7. Dependence-Adjusted Effective Independence

7.1 Dependence Graph

For each pair (i,j), the compounding dependence is:

D_{ij} = 1 - Π_{c ∈ C} (1 - ρ_c(i,j))

where C = {funding, jurisdiction, personnel, supply}.

7.2 Bounded Dependence-Adjusted Heuristic

We define:

n_eff^(dep) = n/(1 + D̄), D̄ = (1/n) Σᵢ Σ_{j≠i} D_{ij}

This is a bounded heuristic, not a spectral measure. It is classified explicitly as a dependence-adjusted screening tool.

7.3 Spectral Construction via Effective Resistance

For a genuinely spectral construction, we use the effective resistance of the dependence graph. Let L = D_diag - D be the Laplacian of the dependence graph, and let L⁺ be its Moore–Penrose pseudoinverse. The effective resistance between nodes a and b is:

R_ab = (e_a - e_b)ᵀ L⁺ (e_a - e_b) 

By Foster's Theorem, Σ_{edges} w_ab · R_ab = n - 1 . We define the spectral effective independence as:

n_eff^(spec) = n/(1 + R̄)

where R̄ is the average effective resistance. This construction is bounded in [1,n] and correctly accounts for graph structure.

7.4 Complete Worked Example

For five authorities with a complete symmetric dependence matrix D ∈ [0,1]⁵ˣ⁵:

D = [[0, 0.96, 0.50, 0.90, 0.85],
[0.96, 0, 0.60, 0.95, 0.70],
[0.50, 0.60, 0, 0.48, 0.55],
[0.90, 0.95, 0.48, 0, 0.81],
