D̄ = (1/5) · Σᵢ Σ_{j≠i} D_{ij} = (1/5) · (14.24 + 15.21 + 10.13 + 14.14 + 12.91) = (1/5) · 66.63 = 13.33

n_eff^(dep) = 5/(1 + 13.33) = 5/14.33 ≈ 0.35

This is below 1, indicating severe effective centralization. The governance implication is:

If n_eff < k, then the system is effectively centralized despite nominal multi-party authorization.

7.5 Falsification Test

The independence model is falsified if median n_eff^(dep) < 2.5 across 10 realistic authority sets.

