Appendix D. Availability Model Derivation

D.1 Latency Distribution

Let $L_i$ be the latency between authority $i$ and the coordinator. Assume $L_i$ has cumulative distribution $F_{L_i}(\ell)$ estimated from empirical traces (inter-AZ, inter-region).

D.2 Quorum Response Probability

For a quorum $Q$ with weight $w(Q) \geq \Theta$, the probability that all members respond within $T_{\text{grace}}$ is:

P(Q \text{ responds}) = \prod_{i \in Q} F_{L_i}(T_{\text{grace}}).

The probability that exactly quorum $Q$ responds (and no others) is:

P(\text{exactly } Q) = \prod_{i \in Q} F_{L_i}(T_{\text{grace}}) \prod_{j \notin Q} (1 - F_{L_j}(T_{\text{grace}})).

Summing over all quorums:

P_{\text{quorum}}(T_{\text{grace}}) = \sum_{Q : w(Q) \geq \Theta} \prod_{i \in Q} F_{L_i}(T_{\text{grace}}) \prod_{j \notin Q} (1 - F_{L_j}(T_{\text{grace}})).

D.3 Correlated Partitions

When failures are correlated (e.g., same availability zone), the independence assumption fails. Let $\mathcal{Z}$ be a partition of authorities into zones. For zone $z \in \mathcal{Z}$, let $F_{L_z}$ be the zone-level latency distribution. Then:

P_{\text{quorum}}(T_{\text{grace}}) = \sum_{Q : w(Q) \geq \Theta} \prod_{z \in \mathcal{Z}} P_z(Q, T_{\text{grace}})

where $P_z(Q, T_{\text{grace}})$ accounts for intra-zone correlation. This is the AWARE-style correlated-partition model adapted to authorization renewal.

D.4 Governance Availability–Safety Frontier

Define:

· $P_{\text{false HALT}}(T_{\text{grace}})$: probability of halting due to transient partition.
· $P_{\text{unsafe run}}(T_{\text{grace}})$: probability of running without valid authorization.

The frontier is:

\min_{T_{\text{grace}}} \left[ c_1 P_{\text{false HALT}}(T_{\text{grace}}) + c_2 P_{\text{unsafe run}}(T_{\text{grace}}) \right]

subject to $T_{\text{grace}} \geq 0$.

Proposition D.1. If $P_{\text{false HALT}}$ is decreasing in $T_{\text{grace}}$ and $P_{\text{unsafe run}}$ is increasing in $T_{\text{grace}}$, then the optimal $T_{\text{grace}}^*$ satisfies:

c_1 \frac{\partial P_{\text{false HALT}}}{\partial T_{\text{grace}}} + c_2 \frac{\partial P_{\text{unsafe run}}}{\partial T_{\text{grace}}} = 0.

Proof. First-order optimality condition. $\square$

D.5 Falsification

The lease model is falsified if $T_{\text{grace}}^* = 0$ for all realistic cost ratios $c_1/c_2$.

