Appendix G. Governance Gap Measurement Protocol

G.1 Corpus Construction

The corpus consists of $N = 80$ institutional interpretations:

· $N_{\text{EU}} = 30$ EU AI Act Article 51 interpretations
· $N_{\text{US}} = 30$ US Executive Order 14110 interpretations
· $N_{\text{UK}} = 20$ UK AI Safety Institute interpretations

G.2 Labeling

Qualified legal experts independently label each scenario $x$ as $y_x \in \{\text{permitted}, \text{prohibited}\}$.

G.3 Inter-Rater Reliability

Krippendorff's $\alpha$:

\alpha = 1 - \frac{D_o}{D_e}

where $D_o$ is observed disagreement and $D_e$ is expected disagreement. Require $\alpha \geq 0.80$.

G.4 Translation

Two translators:

1. Hand-written baseline: Rego or CEL policy authored by a formal-methods engineer.
2. LLM-translated policy: generated by a frontier language model.

G.5 Metrics

\text{Precision} = \frac{|\text{Permitted}_P \cap \text{Permitted}_d|}{|\text{Permitted}_P|}, \quad \text{Recall} = \frac{|\text{Permitted}_P \cap \text{Permitted}_d|}{|\text{Permitted}_d|}.

G.6 Governance Gap

\Gamma = 1 - \frac{2 \cdot \text{Precision} \cdot \text{Recall}}{\text{Precision} + \text{Recall}}.

G.7 Falsification

· Tractable: hand-written baseline $\Gamma \leq 0.10$ across all jurisdictions.
· Severe: LLM-translated $\Gamma > 0.30$ in at least two jurisdictions.

G.8 Enforcement Gap Extension

Define the enforcement gap:

\Gamma_{\text{enf}} = |\{x : \text{Enforced}(x) \neq \text{Permitted}_P(x)\}|.

Measured by red-team exercises attempting to bypass CCL controls.

G.9 Attestation Gap Extension

Define the attestation gap:

\Gamma_{\text{att}} = |\{a : \text{Forgeable}(a) \land C_{\text{attack}}(a) < C_{\text{adversary}}\}|.

Measured by attempting to forge attestation with commodity hardware.

G.10 Adoption Gap Extension

Define the adoption gap:

\Gamma_{\text{adopt}} = 1 - \frac{\text{Accelerators with CCL}}{\text{Total high-end accelerators}}.

