Key results:

· Theorem B.1 (Weighted quorum safety): If 2Θ > W + f_max, then w(Q₁ ∩ Q₂) > f_max for any two quorums.
· Lemma (Weighted intersection, Ligate Research): Any two quorums with weight > (2/3)W intersect in > (1/3)W.
· Falsification: The quorum model is falsified if there exists a weight assignment such that (a) two disjoint quorums each have weight ≥ Θ, or (b) 3f_max ≥ W and the system claims to satisfy both safety and liveness.

